WEBVTT

00:00:01.340 --> 00:00:04.520
Ken went with Aru Kenemon, but at least he had me to rescue him.

00:00:04.520 --> 00:00:08.740
Daemon showed up, and that creepy Oikawa dude was just gonna hand Ken over to him.

00:00:08.740 --> 00:00:10.340
That's when I sprang into action.

00:00:10.340 --> 00:00:13.340
We didn't really need the help, but I was glad when the others finally showed up.

00:00:13.340 --> 00:00:17.240
Took him long enough, Daemon could open digital ports any time he wanted to.

00:00:17.240 --> 00:00:20.800
So Kauri said we should send him to the dark ocean instead of the digital world.

00:00:20.800 --> 00:00:24.860
Easier said than done, Ken had to use the dark powers still deep inside him

00:00:24.860 --> 00:00:27.120
to open the gate and banish Daemon from the face of the Earth.

00:00:27.120 --> 00:00:29.030
Now that's what I'd call teamwork.

00:01:26.680 --> 00:01:28.220
Yes, sir. We're organizing and cleaning.

00:01:28.390 --> 00:01:30.000
Any cleaner in the place would be a sofa.

00:01:33.260 --> 00:01:36.760
Yeah, I've already organized that drawer, sir. I've got the paper cuts to show for it, too.

00:01:36.760 --> 00:01:38.560
Sorry, I just need to find something.

00:01:38.560 --> 00:01:39.960
I'll get the bandages.

00:01:39.960 --> 00:01:42.560
But I'm actually gonna miss the office over the holidays.

00:01:42.560 --> 00:01:44.060
It's always so nice and quiet.

00:01:44.060 --> 00:01:44.880
Found it!

00:01:44.880 --> 00:01:46.130
See what I mean?

00:01:46.130 --> 00:01:47.330
There, this is the guy.

00:01:47.330 --> 00:01:47.990
Ooh.

00:01:47.990 --> 00:01:48.980
He gives me the willies.

00:01:48.980 --> 00:01:50.480
Huh? It is him!

00:01:50.480 --> 00:01:52.910
Well, he was at work until just a few days ago.

00:01:52.910 --> 00:01:56.900
But yesterday and today, he didn't show up at all. He didn't even call in or anything.

00:01:56.900 --> 00:01:59.740
Thanks, Dad. Would it be all right if we kept this picture?

00:01:59.740 --> 00:02:00.000
Of course.

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:01.350
Of course, go right ahead.

00:02:01.350 --> 00:02:03.300
But don't do anything dangerous, okay?

00:02:03.300 --> 00:02:04.330
Uh-huh.

00:02:04.330 --> 00:02:07.540
Hmm, why do I think that's exactly what you're going to do?

00:02:07.540 --> 00:02:10.050
He looks just like an ordinary person.

00:02:10.050 --> 00:02:13.850
Yeah? Then why is he able to control Arokenymon and Mummymon?

00:02:13.850 --> 00:02:16.800
I don't care what he is. I just want to shut him down.

00:02:16.800 --> 00:02:19.020
Ah, Mount Fuji.

00:02:19.020 --> 00:02:23.760
This world can be beautiful, but soon I'll claim my true prize.

00:02:23.760 --> 00:02:26.870
Arokenymon? I believe that opens in.

00:02:26.870 --> 00:02:28.980
Well, it does now.

00:02:31.020 --> 00:02:33.420
If you're through playing around, it's time to get to work.

00:02:33.770 --> 00:02:36.830
This is a classic case of mass hallucination, plain and simple.

00:02:36.830 --> 00:02:39.330
What are you talking about? Buildings have been destroyed!

00:02:39.330 --> 00:02:42.530
It's obviously a government conspiracy to cover up a UFO crash!

00:02:42.530 --> 00:02:46.330
What I'm saying, I mean, I'm just saying that the destruction is real,

00:02:46.330 --> 00:02:50.630
but a mass hallucination caused it to seem that the destruction was caused by monsters.

00:02:50.630 --> 00:02:52.630
The government got to you too, didn't it?

00:02:52.630 --> 00:02:56.030
Oh, if only Digimon were this deluded.

00:02:56.380 --> 00:02:59.510
The digital world would fall at our feet like a ripe little plum.

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:03.120
To them, Digimon and UFOs are exactly the same thing.

00:03:03.120 --> 00:03:05.380
It's just something they're afraid to admit exists.

00:03:05.380 --> 00:03:08.660
But think, if there's such a commotion now,

00:03:08.660 --> 00:03:11.860
wait till all those dark spores begin to bloom.

00:03:14.180 --> 00:03:16.770
Here we go. I'm all done.

00:03:18.470 --> 00:03:22.400
Are you saying that you're done with your homework for the whole winter break?

00:03:22.400 --> 00:03:24.950
Mm-hmm. Honey, that's amazing.

00:03:24.950 --> 00:03:27.220
I'll say it is. Crazy, even.

00:03:27.220 --> 00:03:30.000
I mean, he was just returned from that whole kidnapping incident

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:33.600
last night that's because he's such a smart little boy you know the press is

00:03:33.600 --> 00:03:36.720
sure to show up again to talk about the kidnapping and we can get more attention

00:03:36.720 --> 00:03:41.750
by telling them how smart he is hon maybe he'll become a media darling just

00:03:41.750 --> 00:03:46.590
like that Ken Ichijoji and then we'll get on TV you bet then everyone will

00:03:46.590 --> 00:03:56.270
know we're the parents of a genius in sex yes that's the man all right hmm he

00:03:56.270 --> 00:04:00.000
gives me the willies yeah that's what everybody says about him hey

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:01.400
Didn't you need to be someplace?

00:04:01.400 --> 00:04:02.600
You're right!

00:04:03.470 --> 00:04:04.970
Fill me in when I get back, okay?

00:04:05.280 --> 00:04:07.290
Now feel free to make yourselves at home.

00:04:07.290 --> 00:04:07.990
Thanks!

00:04:08.650 --> 00:04:09.450
See you later!

00:04:10.190 --> 00:04:10.910
Oh, wait.

00:04:11.550 --> 00:04:12.050
Here.

00:04:12.050 --> 00:04:12.520
Hmm?

00:04:13.560 --> 00:04:15.860
Looks like Mom's done some investigating of her own.

00:04:16.370 --> 00:04:16.870
Huh?

00:04:16.870 --> 00:04:19.470
Didn't you know TK's mom is a newspaper reporter?

00:04:19.700 --> 00:04:20.200
Really?

00:04:20.970 --> 00:04:21.470
Yeah.

00:04:21.670 --> 00:04:22.270
And look!

00:04:22.470 --> 00:04:22.970
Wow!

00:04:23.170 --> 00:04:24.270
Uh, what is it?

00:04:24.470 --> 00:04:25.980
Oh, is it a grocery list?

00:04:25.980 --> 00:04:28.680
No, Goofy, it's the names and addresses of the kidnapped kids.

00:04:28.680 --> 00:04:30.000
Your mom does good work.

00:04:30.030 --> 00:04:30.530
D.K.

00:04:30.530 --> 00:04:31.410
Ken?

00:04:31.410 --> 00:04:33.920
We've got to save them all before it's too late.

00:04:33.920 --> 00:04:39.320
We can't allow those children to become drawn into evil the way I was.

00:04:39.320 --> 00:04:41.320
Right! All those kids are depending on us!

00:04:41.320 --> 00:04:42.320
Yeah!

00:04:42.320 --> 00:04:45.840
Hey, I don't mean to cause trouble, but just what is the plan anyway?

00:04:45.840 --> 00:04:47.340
Well, um...

00:04:47.340 --> 00:04:49.340
Let's split up and go meet with those kids.

00:04:49.340 --> 00:04:52.530
If we act quickly, maybe we can stop the dark spores from growing.

00:04:52.530 --> 00:04:55.250
What are we waiting for? Let's go!

00:04:55.250 --> 00:05:00.000
That Noriko girl should be home any time now, right?

00:05:00.030 --> 00:05:00.480
Right.

00:05:00.480 --> 00:05:06.460
Guys, isn't that her, like, right in front of us?

00:05:06.460 --> 00:05:07.960
Oh, yeah.

00:05:07.960 --> 00:05:10.360
She doesn't look so evil playing with that cat.

00:05:10.360 --> 00:05:13.990
Get away from me! You're disgusting!

00:05:14.990 --> 00:05:16.490
She kicked it!

00:05:16.490 --> 00:05:18.560
I guess she is evil, huh?

00:05:18.560 --> 00:05:21.030
Yeah, maybe it's not even worth talking to her.

00:05:21.030 --> 00:05:23.730
It looks like the Dark Spore has already taken hold.

00:05:23.730 --> 00:05:28.020
We have to at least try.

00:05:28.020 --> 00:05:30.000
I don't even like to fight Digimon.

00:05:30.410 --> 00:05:33.350
What will we do if we're forced to fight other kids?

00:05:33.350 --> 00:05:36.650
What do you want?

00:05:36.650 --> 00:05:40.120
No! Now go away and don't come back!

00:05:40.120 --> 00:05:43.390
Wait ma'am, just listen for a minute!

00:05:43.390 --> 00:05:46.900
Ma'am, how do people get any encyclopedias sold?

00:05:46.900 --> 00:05:48.810
Sorry guys, I tried!

00:05:48.810 --> 00:05:51.510
I know, Davis, it's not your fault she got angry.

00:05:51.510 --> 00:05:53.480
Yeah!

00:05:53.480 --> 00:05:54.250
Mmm!

00:05:54.250 --> 00:05:55.820
She needs some catnip!

00:05:55.820 --> 00:05:57.590
Well, let's try the next one!

00:05:57.590 --> 00:06:00.000
Insect!

00:06:00.540 --> 00:06:02.460
Stupid little meaningless bugs.

00:06:02.460 --> 00:06:04.700
They need to be squashed.

00:06:04.700 --> 00:06:09.320
Okay, I'll throw in some oysters, broccoli, a quart of buttermilk,

00:06:09.320 --> 00:06:11.320
and just a dash of vinegar.

00:06:15.890 --> 00:06:18.890
Why do people find this cold wet gunk pretty?

00:06:18.890 --> 00:06:20.890
Do you think it'll cause any problems tomorrow?

00:06:20.890 --> 00:06:22.890
Well, I suppose anything's possible, Arakenemon.

00:06:22.890 --> 00:06:24.810
Go put the snow chains on the tires.

00:06:24.810 --> 00:06:26.810
What? Why should I?

00:06:26.810 --> 00:06:28.770
Because you're annoying me.

00:06:28.770 --> 00:06:29.510
Fine.

00:06:31.820 --> 00:06:33.430
Because you're annoying me.

00:06:33.430 --> 00:07:00.000
I know you're going to hate hearing this, but I really don't think we're going to be able to remove the dark spores from those kids.

00:07:00.190 --> 00:07:04.870
kids. I'm thinking that Oikawa is probably the only person that can extract

00:07:04.870 --> 00:07:09.650
them, but we may be able to use that to our advantage. He's probably got something

00:07:09.650 --> 00:07:13.030
specific planned and will come for them sooner or later, so...

00:07:13.030 --> 00:07:15.770
So if we watch them, we'll catch Oikawa.

00:07:15.770 --> 00:07:17.140
Right.

00:07:17.140 --> 00:07:20.720
That's a great idea! We can ask Tai and the others to help us out, too!

00:07:20.720 --> 00:07:21.830
Sounds good!

00:07:21.830 --> 00:07:25.530
I'm sorry, Kin. I know you'd hoped we could save those kids before...

00:07:25.530 --> 00:07:27.970
You really don't need to worry about me. I'll be fine.

00:07:27.970 --> 00:07:30.000
Mm-hmm.

00:07:31.280 --> 00:07:33.750
It's from my brother.

00:07:33.750 --> 00:07:36.750
Alright! Let's get started on this plan, guys!

00:07:36.750 --> 00:07:39.670
They are nearby. I can sense it.

00:07:39.670 --> 00:07:43.640
Perhaps now I will finally find the answers I seek.

00:07:43.640 --> 00:07:49.340
My teddy bear, mine!

00:07:49.340 --> 00:07:55.680
I told you, you can't have it!

00:07:55.680 --> 00:07:57.790
Hey, you lazybones! Wake up!

00:07:57.790 --> 00:07:59.640
What? Uh...

00:08:00.060 --> 00:08:02.020
We have a visitor. Find out who.

00:08:02.020 --> 00:08:03.020
Teddy Bear?

00:08:09.380 --> 00:08:22.850
Hello?

00:08:22.850 --> 00:08:25.850
Okay, everybody's got their assignments about who they're supposed to follow.

00:08:25.850 --> 00:08:27.320
Make sure you stick close to them.

00:08:27.320 --> 00:08:30.000
We don't want Oikawa sneaking in when we're not looking.

00:08:30.120 --> 00:08:33.120
Following those kids, Ty and Kari are going to the digital world.

00:08:33.120 --> 00:08:34.580
Okay, see you soon!

00:08:36.900 --> 00:08:38.870
Look at all this destruction.

00:08:38.870 --> 00:08:41.550
Any idea what caused it?

00:08:41.550 --> 00:08:42.050
No.

00:08:42.050 --> 00:08:44.170
Hey! Ty! Kari!

00:08:44.170 --> 00:08:48.320
Sorry to call you into the digital world like this, but you're in real serious danger.

00:08:48.320 --> 00:08:50.190
You know who is up to something.

00:08:50.190 --> 00:08:51.180
Twitch my tail!

00:08:51.180 --> 00:08:54.230
You don't mean... not Black War Greymon.

00:08:54.230 --> 00:08:55.730
Mm-hmm.

00:08:55.730 --> 00:09:00.000
Remember when Azulangmon gave up some of his power to help us fight in the real world?

00:09:00.000 --> 00:09:04.310
world? Well when Chennai gave that power to all of us, the defenses of the

00:09:04.310 --> 00:09:08.630
digital world were weakened. With the balance thrown off here, there's not much

00:09:08.630 --> 00:09:12.840
that can stand in the way of Black War Greymon. I guess we've got no choice but

00:09:12.840 --> 00:09:21.120
to try and find a way. Is it? Looks like Mount Fuji. That's because it is Mount Fuji.

00:09:21.120 --> 00:09:24.770
Do you mean that Black War Greymon is in the real world?

00:09:24.770 --> 00:09:30.000
That's what Azulonmon told us. We knew we had to call you guys. But we

00:09:30.480 --> 00:09:31.730
to defeat him.

00:09:31.730 --> 00:09:34.480
Agumon got more power from a Zoolongmon,

00:09:34.480 --> 00:09:36.650
but there wasn't enough power for anyone else.

00:09:36.650 --> 00:09:37.590
Mm-mm.

00:09:37.590 --> 00:09:40.500
Do you think you're up to fighting Black War Greymon, buddy?

00:09:40.500 --> 00:09:42.520
If he really, really wants to.

00:09:42.520 --> 00:09:43.600
All right, then.

00:09:43.600 --> 00:09:45.140
Let's go find him, guys.

00:09:45.140 --> 00:09:47.140
Be careful with Black War Greymon,

00:09:47.140 --> 00:09:49.520
but you can't let him win!

00:09:49.520 --> 00:09:53.560
So, we meet again.

00:09:53.560 --> 00:09:56.120
And this time, we're ready for you.

00:09:58.180 --> 00:10:00.000
Ready to be defeated again, you guys.

00:10:01.760 --> 00:10:04.260
So this is the infamous Black War Greymoor.

00:10:04.260 --> 00:10:06.970
Just what do you hope to accomplish here?

00:10:06.970 --> 00:10:09.370
I wish to look upon the face of my creator.

00:10:11.460 --> 00:10:14.830
You've come all this way to see what you've already seen then.

00:10:14.830 --> 00:10:18.340
I gave you life from just the tiny hairs on my head.

00:10:18.340 --> 00:10:20.340
Perhaps, but who gave you life?

00:10:20.340 --> 00:10:21.320
Huh?

00:10:21.320 --> 00:10:24.120
And who is your creator, Mummymon?

00:10:24.120 --> 00:10:25.770
Oh, well it all.

00:10:25.770 --> 00:10:26.770
It was me.

00:10:26.770 --> 00:10:27.850
Huh?

00:10:27.850 --> 00:10:30.000
I made both of these DJs.

00:10:30.280 --> 00:10:33.520
by turning my DNA into data.

00:10:33.520 --> 00:10:35.430
So you see, Black War Greymon,

00:10:35.430 --> 00:10:37.690
I am the creator you've been searching for.

00:10:37.690 --> 00:10:39.670
- Then I am a product of the real world,

00:10:39.670 --> 00:10:41.110
not the digital one.

00:10:41.110 --> 00:10:42.170
Interesting.

00:10:42.170 --> 00:10:45.370
- Yes, I think you've gotten what you came for, haven't you?

00:10:45.370 --> 00:10:47.690
So now leave us.

00:10:47.690 --> 00:10:50.020
- It's all beginning to make sense to me now.

00:10:50.020 --> 00:10:52.280
I've been searching for answers in the digital world,

00:10:52.280 --> 00:10:54.920
trying to find the meaning of my existence,

00:10:54.920 --> 00:10:57.780
but have been able to find nothing to ease my pain.

00:10:57.780 --> 00:10:59.670
And now I know why.

00:11:00.060 --> 00:11:04.100
I was created from you, just like Arukenimon and Mummymon were.

00:11:04.100 --> 00:11:08.680
We're a part of the real world, foreign to the digital world.

00:11:08.680 --> 00:11:11.360
We do not belong there.

00:11:11.360 --> 00:11:13.990
If you're done philosophizing, then goodbye.

00:11:13.990 --> 00:11:15.580
I'll leave.

00:11:15.580 --> 00:11:20.550
As soon as I'm done here, foreign objects must be eliminated.

00:11:20.550 --> 00:11:21.550
What are you talking about?

00:11:21.550 --> 00:11:23.150
I'm not a foreign object.

00:11:23.150 --> 00:11:24.150
But you are.

00:11:24.150 --> 00:11:26.820
You belong in neither the digital world nor the real world.

00:11:26.820 --> 00:11:28.500
You upset the balance of both.

00:11:28.500 --> 00:11:30.000
This guy's talking crazy.

00:11:30.000 --> 00:11:33.300
Do you want me to, uh, take care of him for you, boss?

00:11:33.300 --> 00:11:35.130
Boss?

00:11:35.130 --> 00:11:37.810
A foreign object?

00:11:37.810 --> 00:11:41.050
I give you life, and this is how you repay me!

00:11:41.050 --> 00:11:42.690
What's going on?

00:11:42.690 --> 00:11:47.640
Aaaaaah!

00:11:47.640 --> 00:11:51.610
You! I remember!

00:11:51.610 --> 00:11:53.200
Let's talk about this!

00:11:53.200 --> 00:11:55.040
There is nothing to talk about!

00:11:55.040 --> 00:11:56.500
Grrrr!

00:11:56.500 --> 00:11:58.160
Hey, look out!

00:11:58.160 --> 00:12:00.000
Pokemon!

00:12:00.350 --> 00:12:01.190
- Digibomb.

00:12:01.190 --> 00:12:07.620
- Woohoo!

00:12:30.380 --> 00:12:32.440
It's going to be a good fight. Maybe we should stay.

00:12:32.440 --> 00:12:34.400
Gatoman, stop him, quick!

00:12:34.400 --> 00:12:53.260
Why do you protect him?

00:12:53.260 --> 00:12:57.320
Because without Oikawa, we'll never get the dark spores out of those kids.

00:12:57.320 --> 00:13:00.000
Don't you understand? They'll stay in there forever if we let you destroy them.

00:13:00.000 --> 00:13:03.510
Then you should have stopped him, not attacked me!

00:13:03.510 --> 00:13:06.010
Don't even think about hurting time!

00:13:06.010 --> 00:13:09.230
Stop her!

00:13:09.230 --> 00:13:11.470
Snake bandage!

00:13:11.470 --> 00:13:20.780
We'd better call the others.

00:13:20.780 --> 00:13:21.780
Right!

00:13:21.780 --> 00:13:23.270
Ta!

00:13:23.270 --> 00:13:25.620
Don't you remember what we talked about?

00:13:25.620 --> 00:13:27.470
We should be working together.

00:13:27.470 --> 00:13:28.470
Never!

00:13:28.470 --> 00:13:29.460
Terrorist!

00:13:29.460 --> 00:13:30.000
Terrorist!

00:13:31.880 --> 00:13:48.710
Watch out!

00:13:48.710 --> 00:13:49.710
Fight when we can be friends.

00:13:49.710 --> 00:13:51.710
Friendship is weakness.

00:13:51.710 --> 00:13:52.710
Fighting.

00:13:52.710 --> 00:13:53.570
Struggle.

00:13:53.570 --> 00:13:54.690
That is my life.

00:13:54.690 --> 00:13:56.690
But it doesn't have to be that way.

00:13:56.690 --> 00:13:57.240
Enough.

00:14:00.480 --> 00:14:06.320
There's no need for two WarGreymons in this world. Either you go, or I go.

00:14:10.230 --> 00:14:11.900
Gangs are here!

00:14:11.900 --> 00:14:14.770
You're just a- Where's David?

00:14:14.770 --> 00:14:16.540
We'd have had to cut off traffic!

00:14:16.540 --> 00:14:19.140
Just a detour, folks. Nothing to see here.

00:14:19.140 --> 00:14:22.460
Yep, just a couple of big digital monsters threatening traffic!

00:14:22.460 --> 00:14:24.600
You heard what the big monster said, folks!

00:14:24.600 --> 00:14:26.630
I just thought of something.

00:14:26.630 --> 00:14:27.560
What's up?

00:14:27.560 --> 00:14:30.000
What happens if the military base gets involved?

00:14:30.990 --> 00:14:33.290
Don't worry, Cody and the others can take care of them!

00:14:33.290 --> 00:14:35.670
ROCK CRACKING!

00:14:35.670 --> 00:14:41.740
For your own good, soldier boys!

00:14:41.740 --> 00:14:49.240
BLAST RING!

00:14:49.240 --> 00:14:50.640
Maybe I should drive.

00:14:50.640 --> 00:14:51.740
Fine.

00:14:53.220 --> 00:14:56.260
So both time, it's three on one out here!

00:14:56.260 --> 00:14:57.970
Let's even the odds!

00:14:57.970 --> 00:14:58.770
SPIDERS RING!

00:14:58.770 --> 00:15:00.000
SNAP AND INCH!

00:15:03.960 --> 00:15:05.200
Take that, brats!

00:15:07.590 --> 00:15:08.890
You can't get away!

00:15:08.890 --> 00:15:10.470
Go get 'em, Pai Oldramon!

00:15:27.160 --> 00:15:29.480
Should we stop them or go after Oikawa?

00:15:30.000 --> 00:15:31.800
Which one's it gonna be, guys?

00:15:31.800 --> 00:15:33.650
Uh, man, I don't know.

00:15:33.650 --> 00:15:35.580
I guess it should be the base.

00:15:35.580 --> 00:15:36.380
Let's go then.

00:15:36.380 --> 00:15:37.480
Chai Ultraman!

00:15:37.480 --> 00:15:38.580
Mega Digimon!

00:15:38.580 --> 00:15:39.580
No!

00:15:41.510 --> 00:15:43.790
Imperial Draman!

00:15:48.240 --> 00:15:54.580
Go!

00:16:02.910 --> 00:16:04.910
You shall face your doom!

00:16:20.450 --> 00:16:27.990
Feel my wrath!

00:16:27.990 --> 00:16:30.000
This is your last chance!

00:16:30.120 --> 00:16:32.120
so eager to fight. I don't know

00:16:32.120 --> 00:16:34.120
but if we fight here at least no one will

00:16:34.120 --> 00:16:35.880
be hurt. So be it.

00:16:36.120 --> 00:16:38.120
Terror Destroyer!

00:16:38.640 --> 00:16:58.480
Thwarted at every turn.

00:16:58.930 --> 00:17:00.000
Our only chance is to run.

00:17:04.440 --> 00:17:06.700
Prices on those jackets. Will you be quiet?

00:17:07.120 --> 00:17:09.280
With all these people around, I can't attack.

00:17:10.620 --> 00:17:11.560
I can.

00:17:13.760 --> 00:17:26.750
He got away.

00:17:27.230 --> 00:17:28.860
That's when we almost had him.

00:17:30.000 --> 00:17:31.600
It's the police. We better get going.

00:17:35.200 --> 00:17:38.550
I'm surprised you could defeat me, even two-on-one.

00:17:39.120 --> 00:17:42.020
Though I almost wish you had destroyed me completely.

00:17:42.160 --> 00:17:44.220
You're kidding me. Is that what you're after?

00:17:44.420 --> 00:17:44.920
What?

00:17:45.130 --> 00:17:49.640
You mean this whole time we've been chasing you around, watching you blow up everything blow-up-able?

00:17:49.640 --> 00:17:51.940
You've just wanted to find something to destroy you?

00:17:52.140 --> 00:17:54.840
Don't you have anything better to do with your free time?

00:17:55.150 --> 00:18:00.000
My life has no meaning. Poor, poor, pitiful me.

00:18:00.480 --> 00:18:05.120
i know all about self-pity when ken was the digimon emperor he treated me like fish bait

00:18:05.120 --> 00:18:09.920
i almost started to believe the awful things he said but deep inside i had faith that someday the

00:18:09.920 --> 00:18:14.320
real ken would come back to me i just kept trying to get through to him i didn't give up and neither

00:18:14.320 --> 00:18:18.960
can you even if your life is all fighting and struggle it can still have meaning i've had to

00:18:18.960 --> 00:18:23.900
fight all my life but i believed in what i was fighting for i think it's that belief not the

00:18:23.900 --> 00:18:30.000
fighting that has given my life meaning can you imagine the trouble ty would get into without me if all you've got

00:18:30.000 --> 00:18:32.780
in your life is lemons, make lemon pie!

00:18:32.780 --> 00:18:34.320
Hey! I'm hungry!

00:18:34.320 --> 00:18:35.000
Hmm...

00:18:35.000 --> 00:18:39.440
And your life doesn't, you know, have to be filled with a whole bunch of incredibly

00:18:39.440 --> 00:18:41.430
amazing events to be special.

00:18:41.430 --> 00:18:46.810
Believe me, some of the best times I've had are just eating, and sleeping, and hanging

00:18:46.810 --> 00:18:47.810
out with my friends!

00:18:47.810 --> 00:18:51.530
And the thing is, we would all be your friends if you just gave us the chance to be!

00:18:51.530 --> 00:18:54.990
He's right. Look at Ken. He never thought he could have friends, and now he has lots

00:18:54.990 --> 00:18:58.130
of them. You just need to lighten up a little, give us a chance.

00:18:58.130 --> 00:18:59.570
I don't know.

00:19:00.250 --> 00:19:02.250
Don't you want some pie?

00:19:02.250 --> 00:19:04.200
This is all so foreign to me.

00:19:04.200 --> 00:19:05.260
I must think on it.

00:19:05.260 --> 00:19:06.260
Are you sure?

00:19:06.260 --> 00:19:08.260
I thank you for your advice.

00:19:08.260 --> 00:19:09.150
You're welcome.

00:19:09.150 --> 00:19:12.150
Perhaps it is time to put aside my warrior ways.

00:19:12.150 --> 00:19:15.040
They have provided me few answers.

00:19:15.040 --> 00:19:18.870
And maybe one day we could even be friends.

00:19:18.870 --> 00:19:20.980
I hope so, BlackwarGreymon.

00:19:20.980 --> 00:19:23.760
I hope so.

00:19:23.760 --> 00:19:25.760
Will BlackwarGreymon find the answers he seeks

00:19:25.760 --> 00:19:28.770
and join the DigiDestined in their quest to defeat the forces of darkness?

00:19:28.770 --> 00:19:30.000
Keep watching today.

00:19:30.000 --> 00:19:32.440
Digital Monsters to find out.
